  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Efficient and Effective Justice (EEJ)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Sri Lanka):  Sri Lanka&apos;s justice system faces a significant challenge with case delays, with some cases taking decades to resolve, delaying the execution of justice. USAID&apos;s Efficient and Effective Justice (EEJ) activity strengthens the justice system by introducing international best practices and improving systems, procedures and the capacity of justice sector actors.With FY 2022 funding, USAID will work closely with the Ministry of Justice and Judicial Service Commission to improve case management systems in courts, as well as improve capacity of judicial and non-judicial personnel in courts and other justice sector institutions, court management systems, and information sharing and user feedback mechanisms.In addition, USAID will support the Bar Association of Sri Lanka, other lawyer associations, and justice sector institutions, such as the Judges&apos; Training Institution and Attorney General&apos;s Department, to adopt and implement standardized programs for continuing legal education, continuing judicial education, and capacity building of non-judicial personnel.  Further, USAID will work with the private sector to introduce and promote Alternative Dispute Resolution mechanisms.USAID will support improving legal education as a long term means of improving the justice sector through producing more skilled legal professionals. For this purpose, USAID will work with law schools to adopt new curricular and teaching methods.Aligning with the US Embassy&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 2.2: &apos;Build support for adherence to rule-of-law, transparency, and inclusive governance.&apos; This activity also supports the USAID Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 1: &apos;Effective Democratic Governance Strengthened.&apos;$2,650,000 funding within this IM contributes to the required DRG directive of $15,100,000.</narrative>
  </description>
